{sov: Notes}
Funk Blueprint: Built on a classic 12-bar dominant blues structure in D
Mixolydian / D Pentatonic featuring Maceo Parker's iconic horn stabs.

Rhythm Comping: Play short, percussive 9th-chord stabs (D9, G9, A9) on the
offbeats, keeping the fretting hand muting tight and bouncy.

The Stop: The signature pauses on beat 1 during the verse require total
silence across the band before James Brown's vocal pickup brings the groove back.

Horn Accents: The brass section provides sharp, syncopated counter-punches
at the end of vocal phrases throughout the 12-bar cycle.
{eov}